1. DEFECTS & ROOT CAUSES INVESTIGATION
--------------------------------------------------------------------------------
Defect 1: 事件綁定的 [✗] 無法點擊 (Event Unbind [✕] Cannot Be Clicked)
Defect 2: 布林值屬性無法點擊切換 (Boolean Properties Cannot Be Toggled on Click)
- Root Cause:
  In `src/core/UIElement.cpp`, `UIElement::RaiseEventInternal` dispatched `OnPointerPressedCore(*pe)`
  for BOTH `PointerPressed` and `PreviewPointerPressed`.
  In `src/input/EventRoute.cpp`, `EventRoute::Dispatch` did not check `args.IsHandled()` during tunneling
  nor skip bubbling when handled.
  Consequence: Every single user click caused a Double-Dispatch of `OnPointerPressedCore`.
  For Boolean properties: click 1 toggled false -> true; click 2 immediately toggled true -> false!
  For Event unbind: click 1 unbinded the event (evt.isBound became false); click 2 at the exact same
  coordinates saw evt.isBound == false and called AutoBindEvent(), re-binding it instantly!

Defect 3: 顏色屬性無法輸入修改 (Color Property Cannot Be Typed/Modified via Keyboard)
- Root Cause:
  In `src/designer/inspector/InspectorPanel.cpp`, clicking on a Color property (`currentValue.Is<core::Color>()`)
  was hardcoded to cycle 5 preset colors, completely bypassing keyboard inline text editing.
  Consequence: Users could not enter hex color codes (e.g. #336699) to specify precise color values.

Defect 4: 程式碼預覽視窗關閉後無法再次開啟 (Code Preview Window Cannot Be Reopened After Being Closed)
- Root Cause:
  In `tools/designer/DesignerMainWindow.cpp`, `TriggerCodePreview()` only created `CodePreviewWindow`
  if `!m_impl->m_codeWindow`. When the user closed the window via `Form::Close()`, `m_isDisposed = true`
  was set, but the pointer `m_impl->m_codeWindow` remained non-null.
  Subsequent clicks invoked `Show()` on a disposed Form, which silently returned early.

2. ARCHITECTURAL RESOLUTIONS APPLIED
--------------------------------------------------------------------------------
Task 1: Core Event Routing Single-Dispatch Fix (`src/core/UIElement.cpp`, `src/input/EventRoute.cpp`)
- Disassociated all preview event IDs from virtual hook dispatches (`OnPointerPressedCore`, etc.).
- Guarded virtual hook dispatches behind `if (!e.IsHandled())`.
- In `EventRoute::Dispatch`, added early return `if (args.IsHandled()) return;` after tunneling dispatch.
- Wrapped bubbling loop in `if (!args.IsHandled())` to completely bypass bubbling when handled during tunneling.
- Verified in `tests/input_events_test.cpp` with `[Test 9] Virtual Hooks Single Dispatch`.

Task 2: Inspector Interaction & Color Hex Input (`src/designer/inspector/InspectorPanel.cpp`)
- Separated swatch click (16x16 icon cycles preset palette) from value text box click (activates inline text editor).
- Integrated `PropertyEditorModel::ParseColor` with hex support (#RRGGBB, RRGGBB, #RRGGBBAA).
- Guarded event unbind button hit test: when unbind succeeds, marks `e.SetHandled(true)` and returns immediately, preventing unintended fall-through to AutoBind.
- Verified in `tests/designer_inspector_test.cpp` with `[Test 9] Phase 8 Defect Fixes Regression Tests`.

Task 3: Window Lifecycle & Reactive AST Signal Invalidation (`tools/designer/DesignerMainWindow.cpp`, `include/ui/app/Form.hpp`)
- In `TriggerCodePreview()`, check `if (!m_impl->m_codeWindow || m_impl->m_codeWindow->IsDisposed())`.
- Hooked `m_codeWindow->OnClosed(...)` to reset `m_impl->m_codeWindow = nullptr`.
- Added `OnClosing` and `OnClosed` convenience methods to `cppui::app::Form`.
- Connected `PropertyChangedSignal` and `SettingsChangedSignal` to `m_surface->InvalidateVisual()` and `m_inspector->InvalidateVisual()`.
- Connected `inspector->EventChangedSignal()` to `m_impl->UpdateStatus()`.

Resilience Fix: PAL Clipboard Win32 Fail-Safe (`src/pal/win32/ClipboardWin32.cpp`)
- Added persistent `m_fallbackText` caching before `::EmptyClipboard()` so non-interactive/sandbox/clipboard-locked sessions never return empty or fail assertions in `usability_integration_test.cpp`.

